  "id": "specific-learning-disorder",
  "term": "specific learning disorder",
  "definition": "Specific learning disorder is a diagnosis in which a person has ongoing, impairing difficulty efficiently and accurately processing information needed for basic academic skills such as reading, writing, or math. It begins during the school years, and the affected skills are much weaker than expected for age or can be maintained only with unusually great effort.",
